--- task
id: t27
dataset: section8
kind: lexical ranking

--- intent
Rank documents by the BM25 relevance of their body to the text `$q`; return the top 10 titles with the score as `s`.

--- params
{"q": "graph databases"}

--- edition2
query about($q: String) {
  match { $d: Doc }
  return { $d.title, bm25($d.body, $q) as s }
  order { bm25($d.body, $q) desc }
  limit 10
}

--- edition3
query about($q: String) {
  match { from bm25({ match { $d: Doc } return { $d } }, $d.body, $q) as $score }
  return { $d.title, $score as s }
  order { $score desc }
  limit 10
}

--- expect ordered edition3
columns: ["d.title","s"]
["The graph primer",2.0232521362860822]
["Rust in production",1.0116260681430411]
["The graph of cities",0.9156193762630337]

--- note
Recorded from the first edition-3 truth on #1316's head, 2026-11-19: the RFC types a `bm25` score as `F64` (`bm25_v1`), where the rows recorded from edition 2 held Lance's `F32` scores. The recorded documents, their order and their scores equal edition 2's rows at `F32` width (each score rounds to edition 2's value); only the score's width differs.
